(Q1) What is a bash shell script? Give one example

A Bash shell script is a text file containing a series of commands written in the Bash scripting language, which is executed by the Bash shell (the default command interpreter in many Linux systems). It automates tasks, runs commands sequentially, and can include programming constructs like loops, conditionals, and variables.


                             








