(Q9) How can you debug a shell script? Give two methods.
         Debugging in shell scripting is essential when your script isn't working as expected. Bash provides several built-in ways to help you trace and diagnose problems.
     Method 1: Use the -x option (Execution Trace)
                This runs the script in debug/trace mode, printing each command and its arguments as they are executed.
     Method 2: Use set -x and set +x for partial debugging
                  Use this when you want to debug only a specific part of the script.
